    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help with a big event im planning. we got a lot of dietary restrictions coming in late for this gala we're doing for a law firm (around 500 people) - mostly severe nut allergies and then a bunch of vegans. what's the best way to communicate this to the kitchen so nothing gets missed and how should we label the buffet so people actually see the warnings?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For communication, send a detailed email to the catering team explaining the dietary restrictions and the need for proper labeling and handling of each dish. Arrange an in-person meeting to discuss and clarify the details, ensuring everyone understands the importance of avoiding cross-contamination.\n\nFor labeling, implement a color-coded labeling system: red for dishes containing nuts, green for vegan dishes, and include a clear legend or infographic to guide guests. Place these labels next to each dish or section on the buffet. Consider using a laser-engraved label or a sign bearing the logos for clarity. Pre-pandemic hotel accommodations often required such careful attention. You might take inspiration from those scenarios and consider preparing a detailed plan appealing to such preemptive precautions.",
